bled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":40,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Only part of the rejection is fixed. Of the three fixes asked for, the package.json change is done, the shrinkwrap change is partial, and `git rm --cached` didn't happen. The sandbox refused `npm install`, `git rm`, `curl`, WebFetch and `tsc -v`, and I didn't work around those refusals. All three acceptance commands pass, but `npx tsc` is still using the global install because `node_modules/typescript` doesn't exist here.\n\n**What I did** (commit `14e0021`, on top of the earlier work-in-progress commit `1eb26a6`, which already had the toolchain, the `.ts` migration and the build wiring):\n- **`package.json`:** added `typescript: \"^7.0.2\"` and `@types/node: \"24.3.0\"` to devDependencies. I used 24.3.0 because the shrinkwrap already pins that version as a dependency of jest, so it needed no new entry.\n- **`npm-shrinkwrap.json`:** I wrote a `typescript` 7.0.2 entry by hand, with its version, download URL and `dev: true`. It has **no integrity hash and no dependency list**, because I couldn't reach the registry and didn't want to make them up.\n- **Interop doc:** added a note on the hand-written entry and on running `git rm --cached` for any emitted `.js` that was committed before its file was migrated.\n\n**Still needed** (needs network and someone allowed to run these, from the repo root):\n1. `npm install --save-dev typescript@^7.0.2`, then commit the refreshed shrinkwrap. This fills the integrity hash and any platform packages TypeScript 7 needs. Until then, `npm ci` may need network to complete the entry.\n2. `git rm --cached DocService/sources/utilsDocService.js`, then commit. The file is still tracked and shows as modified, because the oracle rewrites it on every run. I left that change out of the commit.\n\n**Acceptance results:**\n- `npx tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` passes.\n- `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` passes: 12 suites, 315 tests passed and 1 skipped. It rebuilds the `.js` from the `.ts` first.\n- `npm run lint:check` passes with 0 errors and one existing warning in AdminPanel.\n\n**Decisions** (from the earlier commit, recorded in the interop doc):\n- The `.js` is written next to each `.ts` by `ts-strip.js`, using Node's built-in type stripping, and is not committed (it's in `.gitignore`).\n- `tsc` only type-checks (`noEmit`, `erasableSyntaxOnly`).\n- The oracle, the test scripts, the `prepare` script and the Dockerfile (before `pkg`) all rebuild the `.js` first, so a stale one can't pass the tests on its own.\n- `.ts` files are left out of eslint for now.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- Executor runs need permission for `npm install` and `git rm` (or registry access), or packets that change dependencies can't be finished.\n- `npx tsc` passing tells you nothing if a global TypeScript is installed. The oracle should check that `node_modules/typescript` exists.\n\nI didn't edit the packet file or the friction log, and I created no follow-up packets, because the run rules forbid touching `.theseus/queue/` and `theseus` commands. The earlier work-in-progress commit doesn't record them either. Two still need creating:\n- `.ts` linting with `typescript-eslint`.\n- `Makefile` support for the new build step.","ttft_ms":1402,"type":"result","duration_ms":121162,"uuid":"776a421d-353a-467e-9ddc-a98744731738","ttft_stream_ms":887,"time_to_request_ms":369,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":7,"system_prompt":174,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":44,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":31,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_